# Copy this file to `.env` (beside clew_audio_server.py, or beside the .exe) and edit it.
# `.env` is ignored by git. Command-line options win over this file; this file wins over what
# the last start remembered. No quotes needed, even for a Windows path.

# The folder whose audio files Clew may list and play; several are separated by ";" on Windows
# (":" elsewhere). Each is added to the remembered list, or turned on if it was off.
CLEW_AUDIO_FOLDER=D:\interviews

# The port on 127.0.0.1. Default 47821.
# CLEW_AUDIO_PORT=47821

# A hosted Clew's address(es), comma separated. http://localhost and http://127.0.0.1 are always
# allowed, so leave this out when you run Clew on this computer.
# CLEW_AUDIO_ALLOW_ORIGINS=https://you.github.io

# How long a stream link lasts, in hours. Default 4.
# CLEW_AUDIO_LINK_HOURS=4

# Where the secret's hash and the remembered settings are kept.
# Default: %APPDATA%\clew-audio-server\config.json
# CLEW_AUDIO_CONFIG=

# ffmpeg, for long variable-bit-rate mp3 files (Firefox seeks badly in them, docs/22 section 8): the
# server converts such a file once to a constant-bit-rate mp3, kept in a "cache" folder beside the
# config. A path to ffmpeg, or "off" to never convert. Default: ffmpeg beside this program, else on PATH.
# CLEW_AUDIO_FFMPEG=C:\tools\ffmpeg\bin\ffmpeg.exe
